+## Changed
+
+- Copied `fixture/history/`, `fixture/bad-labels/` and `fixture-rows/` byte-for-byte into `crates/kernel/storage/tests/fixtures/{history,bad-labels,history-rows}/`, hidden `.run/` folders and the blank and malformed `plan.jsonl` lines included.
+- Added `crates/kernel/storage/src/read/snapshot/table_events.rs`: `TableEvent` and the stream/type selection leaf.
+- `EventFacts` now holds `table_events: Vec<TableEvent>`; `Facts::observe` in `read/snapshot/events.rs` keeps each event the tables are built from, in fold order, and nothing else.
+- Added `crates/kernel/storage/src/read/snapshot/records.rs`: `Notice`, `LinkEntry`, `PlanRecord`, `ManifestNotices` and the `serde_json` parsing for `.run/plan.jsonl` and the manifest's `notices` record.
+- `ChangeSnapshot` now holds `plan_records` and `manifest_notices`; `read_change` reuses the manifest value it already reads.
+- Added `read_history`, which reads every archived change then every rejected change in listing order.
+- Re-exported `TableEvent`, `PlanRecord`, `Notice`, `LinkEntry`, `ManifestNotices` and `read_history` from `read/mod.rs` and `lib.rs`.
+- Added `crates/kernel/storage/tests/reading_history.rs` for the five scenarios and `crates/kernel/storage/tests/reading_history_edges.rs` for the stream/type, plan-line and manifest-entry shapes the fixture does not hold.
+
+## Deviated
+
+- The task's Details place the mutation-check cases in `tests/reading_history.rs` but also require every `.rs` file under 250 lines. With the extra cases the file came to 374 lines, so I split them into the new `tests/reading_history_edges.rs` (allowed as a new test file). `reading_history.rs` keeps the five scenarios and is 206 lines; both files are under 250 lines and both test targets run under `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh`.
+- Added a dedicated `parse_manifest_item` in `records.rs`: manifest notice items carry no `folded` field, so they cannot share the plan-notice shape.
+
+## Missing context
+
+- The Details do not say whether the 250-line budget applies to Rust test files; I assumed it does and split accordingly.
+
+## Next
+
